WEBVTT

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:24.350
We may all be different, but we're all here
to protect this body and to carry out our tasks.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.190
What we need to do as the ones left behind

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:33.440
is to keep this body going. The body that
our dear friends risked their lives to protect.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.980
Not destroy it.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.160
"ENUCLEATION CEREMONY"

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.190
The tricuspid valve is about to open.
Red Blood Cells, please do not stop.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.730
Keep the line moving.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.900
And I just got back from a full round
around the whole body.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.100
Why do we even bother punching in?

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.850
Not like the higher-ups take a good look
at our timesheets.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.440
You said it.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.560
We don't get paid time off
or even makeup days.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.690
The only rest we'll ever get is right here.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.940
When the heart comes to a stop.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.400
The heart.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.520
A keystone organ that serves
as the engine for blood circulation.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:49.020
A muscular organ, it constricts
to function as the body's circulatory pump.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.810
Still, the blood vessels seem to be
in even worse shape these days.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.850
It's a chore just to transport this oxygen.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.850
The pathway's beyond bumpy for sure!

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.230
By the way, where's that rookie
you were always with?

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.230
You know, the one with the glasses...

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.650
I haven't been able
to get in touch with him for a while.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.400
His chances of making it back
aren't looking too good.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.560
Well, I can't say I blame him for wanting
to bail on an environment like this.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.850
He did show a lot of promise, though.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.690
Winner of the Top Rookie Award no less.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.310
Don't just stand there!

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.690
Can't you see we're backed up here? Move it!

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.650
S-Sorry!

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.440
Even training an incompetent rookie
is such a chore.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.440
You...

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.060
Um...

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.850
I'm so sorry!

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.980
Man, you really had me worried!

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.020
Been waiting for you, rookie!

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.310
No...

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:04.350
You're a full-fledged
Red Blood Cell now, aren't you?

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.150
Yes!

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.060
Hey! Senpai! Good work!

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.100
I was worried about you,
since I haven't seen you at all lately!

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:19.270
Is that right? Sorry.
I'm fine now, okay?

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.690
Please show me how things are done, all right?

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.600
I'm counting on you.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.690
Right!

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.490
EPISODE 12

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.490
RETURN, THE HEART, AND DEMISE

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.850
Hey, look how fast you are now.
Good pace!

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:07.400
Thank you very much!

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.690
Whoa...

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.730
There's construction going on everywhere!

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.850
Please watch your step.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.400
Thanks for your hard work.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.190
Jeez, could it be any harder to get through?

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.520
Do you even need to do
this kind of construction work?

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.020
We apologize for the inconvenience.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.230
The whole body isn't getting enough oxygen
as it is, so try not to slow us down!

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.940
We're sorry.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.100
No need to apologize!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.690
Since we're only doing what needs to be done!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:37.730
Huh?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:43.350
Haven't you seen enough of it yourself?
Clumps of cholesterol, plaque...

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.850
Plaque.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:51.150
Bump-like piles of built-up
cholesterol and fat.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.350
Differs from dental plaque,
the plaque that builds up inside the mouth.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:59.270
Those things are breaking off
all over the blood vessels!

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:03.440
And fixing all that is our job!

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:07.980
Even still, all this construction work
everywhere we go is a huge pain for us!

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.690
Can't you be more efficient?

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:12.440
Oh, so we should just forget
about the whole thing? Huh?

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:16.600
Why don't you guys deliver that oxygen
more efficiently for heaven's sake?

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.440
Pretty tense, huh?

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.150
Neither of them is really wrong, but still...

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.520
Where to next?

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.980
Uh...

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.100
The next delivery's going to the stomach.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.060
Is something wrong?

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.980
Uh, no.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:37.150
The path to the stomach's pretty clogged,
too, so... Let's be careful on this delivery.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.350
Right!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.970
"MUCUS"

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.650
It's so hot!

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.810
This is my first time here, but who knew
the stomach was such a harsh place?

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:59.020
It seems to be in better shape
than the last time I was here.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.230
Senpai? Are you okay?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.810
I'm okay. Let's go.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.270
Hey! You Red Blood Cells there!

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.150
Get a move on!

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.770
Bring that oxygen here!

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.600
Enough already! Didn't I tell you?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.190
This kind of thing happens
on a daily basis here!

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:44.770
You can't get sentimental every single time,
or you'll end up putting the others at risk!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.730
Oh right! That guy...

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.150
Gastric Chief Cell!

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:54.020
Nice to meet you! I'm NC8429!
I look forward to working with you!

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:55.230
Huh?

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.560
Uh, I wouldn't...

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:59.810
Who the cell has time to remember names?

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.480
Forget that and just get to work!

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.060
W-We're sorry!

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:10.260
"STOMACH"

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:06.730
Come on, let's deliver this oxygen.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.480
R-Right.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:14.560
The same thing happened to me, too,
my first time here.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.900
You watched that orientation video, right?

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.060
That's right!

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:23.060
When you come to the stomach
to make deliveries, tell us your names.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.690
It's a lot more pleasant to work
with a familiar face

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:29.480
than with someone
you don't even know by name.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:32.480
We'll be waiting for you guys!

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.060
See, that video's really, really old.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:36.690
Is that right?

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.100
We should let them know
that they need to make a new one.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.100
Hey, you there!
Quit jawin' and get to work!

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.810
Deliver that oxygen!

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.060
Sorry.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:50.150
You work hard now, AA2153.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.980
Right.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.980
Huh?

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:57.310
Good for you for making it back.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:59.060
Right!

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:03.150
That's amazing! He remembers
your name, huh, Senpai?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:11.020
The truth is, I still didn't know...

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.980
We've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.270
Oh, thanks for your hard work.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:19.900
...what it truly meant to work.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:21.940
Here's your oxygen!

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:23.940
You work so hard every day.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.600
No.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.230
But...

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.350
Since this is...

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.850
...my job!

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.150
Excuse me!

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:39.020
I'm going to try...

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.940
...to give it my all one more time.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.310
All right, we've spotted the germs!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.940
Let's get this over with fast.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.600
Since we need to make up
for our blunder during the gout battle.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.900
Don't let your guard down.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.230
Copy that!

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.690
Hey, this is a breeze!

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.310
Look out!

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:14.310
That was close!

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:17.940
Watch your back.
The shape this body's in...

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:20.350
Germs aren't the only enemy now.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.060
What's up with this place?

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.060
It's bursting with plaque!

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.940
It's getting worse and worse, huh?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:33.020
Watch your step, okay?
We'll have to transport them one by one.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.350
Okay.

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:39.400
Finally made it through.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:42.940
But still...

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.770
...for the coronary arteries,
which carry blood to the heart,

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.560
to end up like this...

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.350
This is no joke.

